"<strong>Wave driver</strong>: a voice coil bolted at the post pushing its own {#} g moving mass and the plate, x = F_c/({#}/G − m ω²), with G the plate's point receptance at the post; stroke limit {#} mm, full drive {#} N (estimates from PASCO's stated millimeter amplitudes at {#} Hz). <strong>Point force</strong>: an ideal force on a free plate. Every mode has the same Q.",
"Sand: where |a| > g a grain is launched at v = (g/ω)√(Γ² − {#}), flies 2v/g and hops randomly with a drift toward smaller |a|; where |a| < g it stays put. Plates are {#} cm across, about {#} mm thick; steel E = {#} GPa, ρ = {#} kg/m³, ν = {#}.",
"<strong>Bar</strong> (Fletcher and Rossing, The Physics of Musical Instruments, ch. {#}): an Euler–Bernoulli beam free at both ends. Modes cosh βx + cos βx − σ(sinh βx + sin βx) with cos βL cosh βL = {#}, f = (βL)² (h/L²)√(E/{#}ρ)/{#}π: βL = {#}, {#}, {#}, {#}, so f₂/f₁ = {#}, f₃/f₁ = {#}. The same modal sum, sand and drive as the plates. Left out: shear and rotary inertia, twisting, bending across the width.",
"<strong>Drumhead.</strong> Ideal membrane σ ∂²w/∂t² = T∇²w clamped at its rim, with no bending stiffness and no air loading: Mylar {#} mm thick (chosen) at {#} kg/m³, σ = {#} kg/m², tension {#} to {#} N/m, c = √(T/σ). Square: f = (c/2L)√(m² + n²); circle: f = j_nm c/({#}πa) with the Bessel zeros {#}, {#}, {#}, {#}, …, so f({#}, {#}) = {#} f₁. A point drive is singular on a membrane, so the drive is a {#} cm pad or a loudspeaker pushing the whole head (the modal mean)."
